WEBVTT

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:07.690
Kaji-kun sounds fiercer than usual.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.820
Could this be... a new Kaji-kun?!

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:13.340
That's it! A new Kaji-kun has been born!

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.280
<i>This is like a good kid
trying to be rebellious.</i>

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:23.410
<i>This is hard.</i>

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:26.680
<i>My arms are screaming.
They feel like they're going to cramp up!</i>

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:29.430
<i>There's slack in one of the strings.</i>

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.220
<i>It broke.</i>

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.610
<i>My third string broke.</i>

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:08.340
<i>What do I do? What do I do?!</i>

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.820
That's the end, it seems.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:46.500
Those Snow White Notes

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.690
Wow!

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.160
<i>With only two strings...</i>

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:15.550
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:19.260
<i>My heart shattered but now I'm feeling calmer.</i>

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:20.800
Kaji-kun!

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.270
You can do it!

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.390
That's amazing...

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:30.480
<i>Even if one of the strings breaks,
you can compensate for it.</i>

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:35.400
<i>However, it takes real skill to change
your technique on the fly like that.</i>

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.170
<i>Of course, producing the
proper sound isn't possible.</i>

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:43.010
<i>The loss of a string robs the futozao
of its intensity,</i>

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:44.460
<i>and its characteristic sound is lost.</i>

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.190
<i>He's carrying on with two strings.</i>

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:51.910
<i>His sound is struggling awkwardly...
There's a limit to what he can do.</i>

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:56.480
<i>But it's impressive that
he didn't just stop playing.</i>

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:00.750
<i>He might look like a puppy dog,
but he's an impressive guy.</i>

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:05.230
<i>I'll probably come dead last.</i>

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:07.870
<i>I know that.</i>

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:10.790
<i>This fight is already over.</i>

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.450
<i>The scent of wind...</i>

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:24.820
<i>I know that...</i>

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:27.370
<i>but I'm not giving up yet.</i>

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:31.170
<i>Since I'm up here on stage, I want
to see this through to the very end.</i>

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:40.250
<i>Whether he's playing well or poorly,</i>

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:43.470
<i>none of that matters.
It's making my heart race.</i>

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:48.470
<i>His playing after losing the use
of a string is much more like him.</i>

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:55.670
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.450
<i>It sounds good,
even with just two strings.</i>

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:17.030
Kaji-kun, you did good!

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.340
That was the best!

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:28.930
<i>Sympathy for a tragic hero, hm?
No harsh reactions here, then.</i>

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:36.090
He's so cute.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:38.300
That was so moving.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.650
He's captured the hearts of all the girls!

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:43.790
The way he carried on after
his string snapped was amazing.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:46.730
I'm sure they'll give him
a high score for that, right?

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:48.910
Unfortunately, that won't happen.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:50.160
What?

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:53.660
If a string snaps in the middle of
a performance in a tournament,

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:57.400
it's viewed as not properly maintaining the
instrument, so he'll likely get a low score.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:58.590
What?!

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:00.420
But why?!

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.470
Yeah, why?!

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:04.450
Quit being so petty, you jerk
with your tiny mustache!

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:05.130
Hey, calm down...

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.830
T-Tiny?

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:12.760
It may seem harsh, but maintaining your
instrument is a skill top musicians need.

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:16.680
And it's something he himself understands.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:25.730
<i>I blew it.</i>

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:30.080
<i>I blew my chance to duke it
out with Tanuma Souichi.</i>

00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:36.720
Are you stupid?

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:39.870
Who on earth works their strings
so hard striking them like that?

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:43.880
I know. I regret it.

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:52.780
<i>Kaji's faltering but honest performance
got the audience on his side.</i>

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:55.130
<i>It's infuriating!</i>

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:58.300
<i>But I'm never telling </i>him<i> that,
even if my mouth gets split open!</i>

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:01.860
<i>That's your punishment for being cute
and having people fawning over you!</i>

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:07.200
He's good, but it's nothing special.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:11.700
Kaji Takaomi totally took the
audience's energy with him.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:15.960
<i>It's his first tournament.</i>

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:19.640
<i>All I want is for him to give a
performance he's happy with.</i>

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:28.340
<i>The ones to watch out of those left to
play are undoubtedly Tanuma Souichi...</i>

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:29.630
Sawamura Setsu

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:29.630
Tokyo

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.340
<i>And...</i>

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:37.490
<i>I haven't once heard his name in
competitions. No rumors, either.</i>

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:39.930
<i>And yet, for some reason...</i>

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:44.940
<i>Ever since I heard that performance,
I just can't stop thinking about him.</i>

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.940
<i>We will now take a break for lunch.</i>

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:51.950
<i>The afternoon session will begin at 1 pm.</i>

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:56.700
<i>We ask that participants please gather
five minutes before the start time.</i>

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:05.050
<i>I feel like I didn't thank Sakura-chan
properly for the lunch she packed for me.</i>

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:07.630
<i>It's all his fault.</i>

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.300
It's so good!

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:14.680
The salmon's huge!

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:20.390
Huh?

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.120
<i>At a time when I want more power,</i>

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:28.110
<i>this flavor, the hugeness of the filling,
and the seasoning balance of this rice ball...</i>

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:29.900
<i>I feel like this happened before...</i>

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.400
<i>Is it dГ©jГ  vu?</i>

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:41.950
I see you're meditating,
but may I speak with you?

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:48.720
I'll make an exception
just for you, Kousuke.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.010
Why, thank you.

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:53.840
You showing up here is a
pretty big deal, Kousuke.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:56.380
I came to show my support.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:00.190
That's a lie. You never
cheer anyone on, Kousuke.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:04.000
Dad's here, too.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:06.310
Something's got everyone curious.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:08.140
<i>Ryuugen-sensei's here?</i>

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:12.100
What about you? Doesn't
anyone here interest you?

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:17.120
I'm not interested in anyone. Why should I be?

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:23.710
<i>In the world of Tsugaru shamisen,
there is no "top spot."</i>

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:26.310
<i>There's only the reaction of the audience,</i>

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:29.860
<i>plus the fighting spirit and
ambitions of the musicians.</i>

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:34.600
<i>"How high can I elevate my sound?"</i>

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:38.020
<i>"Will I find a way to be myself there?"</i>

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:40.310
<i>When those two heard each others' sounds,</i>

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:44.310
<i>what emotions were born in that moment?</i>

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:57.440
<i>Kaji's performance earlier
is still stuck in my head.</i>

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:01.320
<i>So is Arakawa's stirring performance.</i>

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:03.710
<i>And it's not just those two.</i>

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.580
<i>Everyone has all kinds of different sounds.</i>

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:10.120
<i>I'm sure </i>he<i> does, too.</i>

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.940
<i>And me... What will I play?</i>

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:21.150
Umeko?

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:24.800
Setsu.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:28.140
What you did in the group competition
yesterday was a huge disappointment.

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:33.980
I didn't create this tournament
for boring performances like that.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.390
Listen up.

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:36.910
In the individuals,

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:41.150
you'll use Matsugorou's sound to
wow everyone and bag first place.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.040
Don't decide things for me!

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:45.410
I'll decide how I playвЂ”

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:46.350
No.

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:49.150
You must play Matsugorou's sound.

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:50.420
You have a duty to.

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:52.960
I have no suchвЂ”

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:53.540
You do!

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:57.880
This tournament is called
the "Matsugorou Cup,"

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:00.670
but how many people here
even know about Matsugorou?

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:03.390
Matsugorou was amazing.

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:05.680
His genius was undeniable.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:11.860
But he kept his sound to himself and passed
away without ever letting anyone hear it.

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:18.460
If you don't play it, that sound
will disappear from this world.

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:19.780
Are you okay with that?!

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:25.790
<i>Gramps' sound... will disappear?</i>

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:34.860
You'll bring Matsugorou's sound back to life.

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:43.050
<i>The afternoon session will now begin.</i>

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:47.270
<i>From Kudoku High School in
Hokkaido: Fujiwara Jiro-kun.</i>

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:50.010
Oh! There he is!

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:51.790
Sawamura-kun!

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:54.520
You're up soon!
What are you doing?

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:56.860
Everyone was worried so they waited for you.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:59.080
What everyone's waiting for...

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:00.190
...is Gramps' sound.

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:01.660
Huh?

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:02.840
Was it Umeko?

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:05.340
What did she say to you?

00:12:07.230 --> 00:12:08.450
Hey, Setsu!

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.410
Hey, wait!

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:14.380
Sawamura-kun!

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:17.750
I want to hear your sound, Sawamura-kun!

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:22.210
The sound that now accompanies
my grandma's memories...

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:26.430
My desire to keep playing the shamisen...

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:30.380
Sawamura-kun, <i>your</i> Tsugaru
shamisen made those things happen!

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:32.140
A-And I...

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:36.060
I hate to admit it,
and I don't want to say this,

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.980
but we only got this far because of you!

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:40.160
Setsu-san, I want to hear your sound!

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.220
Sawamura!

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.220
Sawamura-kun!

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.220
Setsu.

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:43.230
Setsu-san!

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:49.990
<i>Contestant Number 36.</i>

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:53.200
<i>From Umezono Academy in
Tokyo: Sawamura Setsu-kun.</i>

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:06.010
Setsu Sawamura!

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:07.810
Go, go! Sawamura!

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:08.370
Come on!

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:09.740
Go, go! Sawamura!

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:10.390
Bring it!

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:11.830
Go, go! Sawamura!

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:12.330
Go!

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:13.740
Go, go! Sawamura!

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:14.520
Yeah!

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:16.110
We're gonna cheer, too!

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:15.880
Go, go! Sawamura!

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:16.300
Come on!

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:17.240
Sawamura!

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:20.270
What we wanna hear is <i>your </i>shamisen playing!

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:21.880
You're a guy who can do whatever he wants!

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:24.300
Go back to being that arrogant character!

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:26.880
Y-You can do it!

00:13:27.650 --> 00:13:28.320
Did...

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:31.000
Did you eat the rice balls?

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:34.640
To repay you for all the happiness I get
from hearing you play the shamisen,

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:37.870
I added in "Be Delicious" power!

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:40.090
What's that mean?

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:40.770
Huh?

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:46.380
He gave quite a performance
in the group competition.

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:50.140
That guy's the real deal, isn't he?

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:51.820
Yeah.

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:55.500
But... I've never heard his name before.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:11.240
Matsugorou was amazing.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:15.710
But he kept his sound to himself and passed
away without ever letting anyone hear it.

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:19.330
<i>From Gramps... to me.</i>

00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:23.340
<i>The spirit of his sound passed away
with him? I won't let anyone say that!</i>

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:31.070
<i>Year on year, the overall tempo
of performances increases.</i>

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:33.690
<i>But amidst all the others'
short, tight bachi strikes,</i>

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:36.560
<i>this child's playing is calm and open.</i>

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:40.140
<i>Whoever taught this child, he had
the touch of a seasoned musician.</i>

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:53.330
<i>It's cool and clear.</i>

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:59.230
<i>Well... Shall we go?</i>

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:14.890
<i>It's fluid.</i>

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:20.480
<i>He's striking, but the sound is supple.</i>

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:23.190
<i>This sound...</i>

00:16:23.050 --> 00:16:24.210
Gramps.

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:29.920
Setsu.

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:31.970
Come here.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:39.480
This damp, melancholy smell
you brought home with you...

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:42.130
Did something bad happen?

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:45.630
Go ahead and cry.

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:48.570
And when you've cried your eyes out, get angry

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:51.240
at whoever the idiots were who did this to you.

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:55.580
I'll play the shamisen for
you as much as you want.

00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:57.240
Then, afterwards...

00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:58.890
Smile.

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:01.750
Gramps.

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.390
Smile.

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:04.380
I...

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:06.590
I...

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:07.460
Get angry.

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:09.210
Gramps, your sound...

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:11.000
Play the shamisen.

00:17:11.390 --> 00:17:13.010
Gramps, your sound...

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.470
Play!

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:24.930
<i>Ah... This isn't it.</i>

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:26.310
<i>It wasn't like this.</i>

00:17:26.990 --> 00:17:29.420
<i>Gramps' sound was more amazing.</i>

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:30.780
<i>Even more...</i>

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:34.360
<i>It changed the world in front of your eyes!</i>

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:41.370
<i>I-Is this really the performance
of a sixteen-year-old boy?</i>

00:17:42.170 --> 00:17:44.840
It's a very simple Shinkyuubushi.

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:49.080
Since I'm all about the flashy stuff,
I should find it boring, but...

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:52.850
<i>It's strange, but it doesn't
feel like it's lacking anything.</i>

00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:56.840
<i>Every single sound is clear and the
rhythm's beautiful, like raindrops.</i>

00:17:57.750 --> 00:17:58.890
Isn't it too plain?

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:01.320
Plain? You think so?

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:06.670
<i>It don't follow the latest trends.
It isn't interesting at all!</i>

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:15.120
Perhaps the air conditioning's
too strong? It's quite cold in here.

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:20.170
<i>So this is Setsu.</i>

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:29.460
<i>No, this is Matsugorou's touch.</i>

00:18:32.470 --> 00:18:34.720
<i>That's it! Just like that!</i>

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:37.900
<i>Take it to the end, Setsu!</i>

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:46.650
<i>They often say a person's life
can be heard in their sound.</i>

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:50.690
That's unreal! It sounds just like old Matsu!

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:53.140
<i>Hey, Gramps.</i>

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:57.150
<i>This dolt Setsu is trying to carry you.</i>

00:18:58.420 --> 00:18:59.960
<i>Deeper and deeper...</i>

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:02.450
<i>Carrying you all the way down.</i>

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:07.670
<i>Hey!</i>

00:19:07.670 --> 00:19:09.120
<i>What's wrong with him?</i>

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:12.050
<i>Was his sound always this mature?</i>

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:16.050
<i>Setsu-san...</i>

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:18.020
<i>Sawamura-kun...</i>

00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:20.210
<i>This is amazing, but something's not right.</i>

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:22.040
<i>Setsu-san...</i>

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:23.860
<i>Sawamura-kun...</i>

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:26.220
<i>It's your usual sound we want to hear!</i>

00:19:28.490 --> 00:19:30.060
<i>It's certainly accomplished.</i>

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:32.360
<i>But this isn't it.</i>

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:34.630
<i>Sawamura is more mercurial.</i>

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:45.160
<i>Why am I here, playing like this?</i>

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:48.600
<i>I was aiming for Gramps' sound...</i>

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:52.380
<i>And here in my first competition,
people want Gramps' sound.</i>

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:11.310
<i>But Gramps has died.</i>

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:18.380
<i>There is no sound.</i>

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:29.900
<i>I can't hear anything.</i>

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:33.620
<i>And yet, even if I can't hear anything...</i>

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:43.660
<i>I have memories and feelings.</i>

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:45.040
<i>Everyone does.</i>

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:51.720
<i>They stack one on top of another,
on top of another, on top of another...</i>

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:53.560
<i>...on top of another.</i>

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:55.980
That was awesome!

00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:59.020
If it's the shamisen that gives you life,

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:03.650
then one day, whether you like it
or not, that world will drag you in.

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:06.030
Offerings

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:12.070
If it was something really important...
Something I'd regret if I didn't do it...

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:14.890
I'd give it my best shot on my
own terms, even if I knew I'd fail.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:20.340
You inherited the living
spirit of his sound, didn't you?

00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:24.470
You see, just now, I wasn't
chasing the sound, I was riding it!

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:27.470
Sawamura-kun, your sound was
leaping so freely, it felt amazing!

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:32.520
We did it! We really did it!

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:35.210
It was amazing! We were amazing!

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:37.770
Ah, I'm on such a post-performance high!

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:39.770
Look! I've got goosebumps!

00:21:42.060 --> 00:21:44.320
Who are you trying to imitate?

00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:48.570
Is that your sound?

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:49.810
Setsu.

00:21:51.480 --> 00:21:54.190
You play the shamisen well.

00:21:54.190 --> 00:21:58.170
But the truth is, you only ever imitate me.

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:04.460
Until you realize how you sound so disgraceful,

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:06.430
you are not allowed to play it.

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:12.190
Use your own sound to steal it.

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:15.690
<i>I know, Gramps.</i>

00:22:17.710 --> 00:22:21.600
<i>It's only an inkling, but I think I've
found the road home to my sound.</i>

00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:31.530
<i>The sound...</i>

00:22:31.530 --> 00:22:32.710
<i>It changed.</i>
